name "jev"
bin "jev"
about "Typed judgments about the input, from a System One model"
long_about #"""
Typed judgments about the input, from a System One model

A System One model answers named questions about a piece of content and returns one typed answer per question rather than text: a yes/no probability (`noul`), a choice among named options with their probabilities (`choice`), an expected score against an ordered rubric (`score`). The input is the content; the answers are values, so a judgment stands in a pipeline as any other step does, and a gate is one whose answer decides what follows.

The service is TypeSafe AI, reached at `$env.TYPESAFE_URL` when set, with the key `$env.TYPESAFE_TOKEN` or `$env.TYPESAFE_API_KEY` as a bearer token. An answer is kept by the request that made it, so the same question of the same content is answered once while the plugin runs.
"""#
cmd ask help="Answer named questions about the input" {
    long_help #"""
Answer named questions about the input

The questions are a record by name, each `{type, instructions?, criteria?}`: `{billing: {type: noul, instructions: "Is this about billing?"}, urgency: {type: score, criteria: ["Can wait" "Today"]}}`. The answer is the service's response: `answers` holds one record per question under its name, typed as the question is, and `usage` the tokens.
"""#
    flag --model help="The model: `jev-latest` unless the flag says otherwise" {
        arg <MODEL>
    }
    arg (record)"<questions>" help="The questions by name"
    output ("record<model: string, answers: record, usage: record<input_tokens: int, output_tokens: int>>")"json" framing="json" default=#true
}
cmd noul help="Whether a yes/no statement holds of the input, as a probability" {
    long_help #"""
Whether a yes/no statement holds of the input, as a probability

One `noul` question, answered as the probability that the statement holds, between 0 and 1.
"""#
    flag --model help="The model: `jev-latest` unless the flag says otherwise" {
        arg <MODEL>
    }
    arg <statement> help="The statement to judge the input by"
    output ("float")"json" framing="json" default=#true
}
